'''''Nymphaea''''' ({{IPAc-en|n|ɪ|m|ˈ|f|iː|ə}}) is a [[genus]] of [[hardiness (plants)|hardy]] and tender [[aquatic plant]]s in the family [[Nymphaeaceae]]. The genus has a [[cosmopolitan distribution]]. Many species are cultivated as [[ornamental plant]]s, and many [[cultivar]]s have been bred. Some taxa occur as [[introduced species]] where they are not native,<ref name=fna>{{efloras|1|122531|''Nymphaea''}}</ref> and some are [[weed]]s.<ref name=jeps>{{Jepson eFlora|id=8797 |taxon=''Nymphaea''}}</ref> Plants of the genus are known commonly as '''water lilies''',<ref name=fna/><ref name=itis>{{ITIS|id=18383 |taxon=''Nymphaea''}}</ref> or '''waterlilies''' in the United Kingdom.

